      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs12.md #11b, 2026-08-06): a partial
      ⍝ shape product legitimately overflows int64 when a later axis is
      ⍝ 0 (the overflowing partial product is intentionally discarded,
      ⍝ per design comments in Shape.hh/Shape.cc) -- but doing that via
      ⍝ plain "volume *= len" made the overflow itself UB rather than
      ⍝ just an intentionally-discarded value. Shape::add_shape_item()
      ⍝ and Shape::fits_into() now multiply via uint64_t (well-defined
      ⍝ wraparound) instead.
      ⍝
      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ 64-bit integers (IBM APL2: 32 bit)
      ⍴ 10000000 100000000000000 0⍴42
10000000 100000000000000 0

      0 = ≢, 10000000 100000000000000 0⍴42
1

      ⍝ regression

      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP
      ¯1⍴0,0
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ¯1⍴0,0
      ^ ^

      )SIC

      ⍝ Bugs28 #32 regression: parse-time constant folding of A⍴B (4+
      ⍝ tokens, e.g. inside ⎕FX-defined function bodies) raised its
      ⍝ errors *while parsing* instead of when the statement actually
      ⍝ runs -- no failed statement/carets were shown, ⎕EM/⎕ET stayed
      ⍝ unset, and ⎕FX refused to define an otherwise syntactically
      ⍝ valid function outright. Parser.cc's optimize_short_primitives()
      ⍝ now validates A (integral, fits ShapeItem, rank ≤ MAX_RANK)
      ⍝ before ever constructing a Shape from it, deferring to the
      ⍝ ordinary (correctly-reporting) runtime path instead of folding
      ⍝ when it isn't. Along the way: ComplexCell::is_near_int()/
      ⍝ is_near_int64_t() considered e.g. 2J1 "int-like" (both parts
      ⍝ independently near-integers) without requiring the imaginary
      ⍝ part be ≈0 -- get_near_int() then threw for the same value one
      ⍝ guard later, in one case (Token.cc's own error-message
      ⍝ formatting) recursing back into the very error-reporting code
      ⍝ the guard existed to protect, and stack-overflowing.
      ⍝
      Z←'2'⍴5
DOMAIN ERROR
      Z←'2'⍴5
        ^  ^

      ⎕EM
DOMAIN ERROR 
      Z←'2'⍴5
        ^  ^ 

      ⎕ET
5 4

      )SIC
      Z←2.5⍴5
DOMAIN ERROR
      Z←2.5⍴5
        ^  ^

      )SIC
      Z←2J1⍴5
DOMAIN ERROR
      Z←2J1⍴5
        ^  ^

      )SIC

      ⍝ ⎕FX must be able to define the function -- the DOMAIN ERROR
      ⍝ belongs to *running* line 1, not to ⎕FX itself
      ⍝
      ⎕FX 'ZZ32F' 'Z←''2''⍴5' 'Z←1'
ZZ32F

      ⎕NC 'ZZ32F'
3

      ZZ32F 5
DOMAIN ERROR
ZZ32F[1]  Z←'2'⍴5
            ^  ^

      )SIC

      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #100(t)): a monadic fold of an already-
      ⍝ simple-scalar B (e.g. ⊂1, where the comment right above this
      ⍝ code says "otherwise ⊂B is B" and correctly leaves B itself
      ⍝ unchanged) never retagged B's own token, unlike a non-scalar ⊂
      ⍝ fold, which does -- so nothing marked "a fold happened here" at
      ⍝ this position, and Executable.cc's error-display reconstruction
      ⍝ (which relies on spotting that marker to know it must show the
      ⍝ un-optimized statement instead of the compacted one) never
      ⍝ triggered: a later error in the same statement displayed the
      ⍝ compacted, ⊂-less text, e.g. (⊂1)↑M shown as (1)↑M.
      ⍝ The left caret is at the (: the error display used to count 3
      ⍝ tokens (as for A⍴B) for the 2 tokens of ⊂B, which put it one
      ⍝ token too far left, at the ←.
      ⍝
      M←2 2⍴⍳4
      Z←(⊂1)↑M
LENGTH ERROR+
      Z←(⊂1)↑M
        ^   ^

      )SIC

      ⍝ control: ⊂B for a non-scalar B was already correctly displayed
      ⍝ before this fix (it already retagged B), and ⊂1 itself (no
      ⍝ error) still computes the same, unwrapped value it always did
      ⍝
      Z←(⊂1 2)↑M
DOMAIN ERROR
      Z←(⊂1 2)↑M
        ^     ^

      )SIC

      ≡⊂1
0

      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs31 #28 and #5): the parse-time
      ⍝ constant folding of a literal A⍴B accepted a negative item of A
      ⍝ (⍴0 ¯2⍴0 was 0 ¯2) while the runtime A⍴B gave DOMAIN ERROR. The
      ⍝ malformed value then made the rank operator's empty-frame path
      ⍝ assert (#28), and made A/B throw std::length_error, which ended
      ⍝ the session (#5). Folded and runtime A⍴B now both give DOMAIN
      ⍝ ERROR.
      ⍝
      ⍴0 ¯2⍴0
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⍴0 ¯2⍴0
       ^   ^

      )SIC
      ⍴0 ¯2 3⍴0
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⍴0 ¯2 3⍴0
       ^     ^

      )SIC
      A←0 ¯2 ◊ ⍴A⍴0
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⍴A⍴0
       ^^

      )SIC
      (⌈/⍤1)0 ¯2⍴0
DOMAIN ERROR+
      (⌈/⍤1)0 ¯2⍴0
            ^   ^

      )SIC
      Z←1 0/0 ¯2⍴0
DOMAIN ERROR+
      Z←1 0/0 ¯2⍴0
            ^   ^

      )SIC
      Z←1/0 ¯2⍴0
DOMAIN ERROR+
      Z←1/0 ¯2⍴0
          ^   ^

      )SIC
      'session still alive'
session still alive

      )ERASE A

      )ERASE M Z

